# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore - MoE FPGA prototype
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Principle: commit only what cannot be regenerated on this machine.
#
# The repository is deliberately small (~640 KB without build output).  Anything
# that a script can rebuild is excluded, because a checked-in artefact goes stale
# silently and then lies about what the source does.
#
# Note on the weight/activation .mem files: they ARE committed, even though
# scripts/gen_mem.py generates them, because Python is broken in this environment
# (exits with 0xC0000409).  A fresh checkout has to work here, so the generated
# data ships with it.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- build output: everything under build/ is regenerable ------------------
# See build/README.md for how to recreate each item.
/build/*
!/build/README.md

# ---- Vivado project and checkpoint artefacts -------------------------------
*.dcp
*.bit
*.ltx
*.str
*.Xil
.Xil/
*.jou
*.pb
vivado.log
vivado_pid*.str
*.backup.jou
*.backup.log
usage_statistics_webtalk.*
tight_setup_hold_pins.txt

# ---- simulator droppings --------------------------------------------------
# scripts/sim.cmd sweeps these into build/logs/<mode>/ after every run; these
# rules are the belt to that braces, for runs started by hand or by Vivado.
/xsim.dir/
/*.wdb
/*.log
/xsim*
/xvlog*
/xelab*
/webtalk*
/.Xil/

# ---- simulation outputs (inputs are kept, outputs are not) ----------------
# sim/data/input.mem and sim/data/ref_out.hex are stimulus and golden reference:
# committed.  These two are produced by the testbenches:
/sim/data/readout_out.hex
/sim/data/rtl_out.hex

# ---- OS and editor noise --------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# ---- diagnostics and golden-model outputs ---------------------------------
# golden.ps1 writes this; it is regenerable in about three seconds.
/sim/data/golden_ps.hex
# tb_loader writes this; it is the 256-lane result of the loader test.
/sim/data/loader_out.hex

# ---- tool caches -----------------------------------------------------------
/.cache/

# ---- capture and archive artefacts ----------------------------------------
# These are throwaway outputs from pktmon and from packaging the tree; they are
# large, machine-specific, and regenerate on demand.
/board.etl
/board.txt
/board.etl.*
/rtl.zip
# temporary commit-message files
/msg*.txt
